# Invariant 6 (DS-1 of the server-half review): an instance Remove nobody commits within its 24 h TTL
# is voided, and the inactivity sweep proposes it again in the same epoch. The external sender signs
# deterministically, so the new proposal is the voided one byte for byte: the instance re-arms it
# rather than failing on the duplicate (and taking it out of its own queue). Carol stays away for 91
# days, her Remove is issued, nobody commits for a day, the void lifts the freeze, and the very
# same sweep re-arms it: alice's send is refused again, and her commit - which references the
# proposal every member holds - is accepted.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=dededededededededededededededede community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
sync carol
go_offline carol
advance_clock 45d
send alice chat nobody is past the window at day 45
expect_decrypts bob chat nobody is past the window at day 45
advance_clock 46d
expect_425 send alice chat carol is past it at day 91
advance_clock 25h
expect_425 send alice chat the voided remove is re-armed
commit alice
send alice chat carol is out
expect_decrypts bob chat carol is out
